WEBVTT

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.700
The reason that Kawachi-san’s dough is not rising

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.740
is probably... endoproteases.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.790
The result of hydrolytic
enzymes that can digest proteins.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.870
The woman bribed the man in black
responsible for bringing in the ingredients,

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:28.000
and Kawachi-san was handed
flour that had a large amount of

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.680
endoproteases added to it.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.050
If such a thing is mixed in large doses,

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.590
nothing, not even Solar Gauntlets,

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.010
would be able to make the flour even firm up.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.060
Shut up, boy!

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.730
It’s not enough to simply win.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:46.390
We must have the cockroaches
of the Southern Tokyo Branch

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:51.490
shamed and crushed before
the owner before they leave.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.820
I know she said that,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.400
but would she really go this far?

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.450
That woman is...

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:05.290
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.170
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.500
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.860
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:17.930
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:21.600
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:39.080
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:47.050
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:54.920
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:01:55.970 --> 00:02:02.640
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:10.110
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:19.490
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:28.250
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.510
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.500
is the light of only you.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.250
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:44.060
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:51.780
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:55.570
The indomitable fighting spirit!

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:57.870
Use adversity as a springboard to success!

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.040
It looks like Kanmuri has figured it out.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.040
But, it’s really hard for me to suppress my laughter.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.430
I... I can’t...

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.680
It’s so funny!

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.480
My expression’s slipping.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.520
I think I’m going to die...

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.520
There’s... something strange going on with Kawachi.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:38.490
He really seems to be taking his time.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.030
So it seems.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:42.570
That Kanmuri person has
already finished molding his bread,

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:44.880
and is beginning the baking process.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:51.580
Maybe... because it’s the
semifinals, he’s doing things carefully.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:52.670
I see...

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.500
What the hell is going on here?

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:02.510
Far from it beginning to rise,
the flour won’t even firm up.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:05.510
The wind...?

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:11.520
Air’s coming in from over there.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.860
That’s right, the temperature!

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.520
It’s not fermenting because
the temperature’s really low here.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:18.610
Kuroyanagi-han.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:19.740
What is it?

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:22.030
The dough’s not fermenting as it should.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.030
It might be that the temperature is low,

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.450
so can we turn up the heating in here for a bit?

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.880
The heating?

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.500
Very well.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.210
You guys are the main show today.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.460
If anything is required in order
for you to bake delicious bread,

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.550
we’ll meet that demand.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.560
I do not think that the temperature of
the room has anything to do with it,

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.560
but something is strange.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:00.990
Like increasing the heat is going to help!

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:04.160
You’re really funny, Blondie.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.500
But stop now, Yukino,

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:11.210
you must not laugh...

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.510
When the fermentation doesn’t go well,

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:26.010
it is the most basic of basics
to raise the room’s temperature.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:28.810
However, Kawachi-san,

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:31.100
your dough is already dead.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:34.020
I’m sorry, but could you raise
the temperature a little more?

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:35.440
Very well.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:46.410
Forgive me, Kawachi-san.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.710
All I can do is to know that...

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:51.580
even if you’d been able to bring out 100%,

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.040
or even 200% of your strength,

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.540
you wouldn’t have been able to win against me.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.130
Not against...

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:02.550
my Pan au algue, made with
the Kaiyou yeast of dreams.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:08.470
It’s gotten pretty hot in here.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:11.060
It’s just like a gym in summer.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:14.560
The room’s temperature has easily passed 40°C.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:18.520
In addition, there are so many
people in such an airtight room.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.570
It’s like being in a sauna.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:24.570
However, even with this, Kawachi’s dough isn’t...

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:27.330
It’s... hot.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.660
Why?

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:31.460
Why won’t it firm up?

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.500
My hands are beginning to go numb...

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:39.460
And my head seems to be... I’m spacing out.

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:47.470
At this rate, I’m going to die laughing.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:52.970
I feel a dark, evil, inhuman
energy coming from that woman.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:57.470
What in the world is she?

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.650
Examiner Kuroyanagi.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:02.570
What?

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:05.030
I’d like for you to taste my bread some time soon,

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:07.950
because in this heat, both my bread and I will...

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.330
Also, that person seems to be at his limits as well.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.700
Don’t like too much heat.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.540
Hate it. Really hate it.

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:22.670
Very well.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:25.920
For now, we’ll judge Kanmuri’s bread first.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.510
Kawachi may continue working.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.470
This is the French specialty bread,

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:38.020
Pan au algue, made with seaweed and Kaiyou yeast.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:42.530
You chose this bread as the best choice for bringing out the effect of the kaiyou yeast, eh?

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:49.240
It’s been known for a long time that
yeasts exist in marine environments.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:52.870
However, unlike in terrestrial environments,

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:55.620
the number of yeasts that
exist in the sea is much smaller.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:01.120
Many researchers have tried to
isolate Kaiyou yeast, and failed.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.050
I was no exception...

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:07.090
Kanmuri!

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:09.420
It’s frustrating that you
managed it before I did,

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:10.510
but I’m grateful that you’ve

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:14.220
presented me with the opportunity of tasting Kaiyou yeast bread with my own tongue.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.230
Three years ago,

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:26.650
I was still a student at Harvard.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.390
Ahh, Cathy.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.970
Your hair was a beautiful blonde

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:01.110
that always shone like silk
in the setting sun.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:04.650
That’s right, it felt just like this.

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:09.820
I’d always caress your silky
hair softly with my left hand,

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:12.110
and with my right hand, I’d
gently put pressure on your nape.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:13.910
And...

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:16.330
a gentle kiss...

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:17.610
Kuroyanagi-kun.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:19.950
I did say that

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:24.620
love is rather like
the chaos found in outer space,

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:28.040
but to think that I was categorized as a target...

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:32.880
The wonderful Pan au algue!

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:36.840
The Kaiyou yeast brought back
a painful memory of the seaside!

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.480
I wonder if the heat got to him.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:45.980
No, I believe that he has
always had that sort of orientation.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:47.900
No, I don’t!!

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:53.200
W-What is it?

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:04.870
Dave stands!!

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:05.660
He stood! He stood!
Dave stands!!

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:06.410
He stood! He stood!

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:09.920
Dave... Dave stood up!!!

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.420
The phonetic points are...?

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.420
It’s...

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.430
The 300 of dreams?!

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:21.430
What is that?

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:21.890
He stood up! He stood up!

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:23.930
You and Koala beat the
newcomers’ record with 225 points,

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:25.890
Dave stood up!

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:26.560
Stood, stood, stoo-ood, stoo-ood.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:30.440
but Dave’s voice is supposedly able to
actually go up to 300 phonetic points.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:33.530
In other words. This is the real...

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:34.440
“perfect score”!

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.320
N-No way...

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.450
Then, no matter what Kawachi does...

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:46.410
W-What...?

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:48.800
I think there was a really loud shout,

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:54.670
but I think it was 225 points with Azuma, right?

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:59.350
Kanmuri was really strong, I guess...

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:05.570
But...

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:10.450
as long as I don’t lose my nerve,
I can get a perfect score at any time.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.020
I won’t lose.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:14.490
I definitely won’t lose!

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:18.910
Man, he’s swaying on his feet.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:22.740
You can’t be passing out yourself
after increasing the temperature so much.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.990
Either way, you won’t be able to win.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:26.040
So, forfeit!

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:27.750
Forfeit!

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:30.330
It’s your loss!

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:31.880
It’s pointless!

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:35.000
Umm... umm... please don’t throw things.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.260
Don’t throw...

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:38.300
I’m telling you not to throw things!

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:39.880
You idiots!

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:41.890
Stop it!

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.890
Don’t bully Kawachi!

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.060
Azuma...

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:49.480
I’m... You see, I’m...

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:53.070
just not talented the way you are.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:56.860
I know.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:59.990
I... know that.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.990
However, I...

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:06.920
I... At least I never lose when it comes to guts.

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.000
For the sake of my family...

00:12:10.460 --> 00:12:11.670
for my own sake...

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:13.510
for Tsukino’s sake...

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:16.800
I can’t lose...

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:22.470
The cockroaches are being run out.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:25.930
This is so heartening.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:29.470
Are you Southern Branch guys
trying to kill me by making me laugh?

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:30.970
Go back!

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:33.700
Tsukino...

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:36.110
I’m sorry.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.530
Kawachi-san!

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:46.330
This is...

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:49.490
Forget about rising,
it hasn’t even firmed up.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:53.000
That woman... what has she done?

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.500
After all that kneading,
it is still in this condition...

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.930
It appears there is need
for an investigation.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:04.000
Please.

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:15.360
Tsukino...

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:16.860
I’m sorry.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:20.110
It’s really pathetic.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.730
I’m a mediocre person.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:25.110
No, I’m below mediocrity.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:27.960
I can’t protect even one woman.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:30.120
I’m really sorry.

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:33.410
I’m sorry, Tsukino.

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:35.120
Oh, you’ve come to, have you?

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.130
You’re pretty muscular,
aren’t you, Tsukino?

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:42.010
There, there.
Now stop crying.

00:13:44.430 --> 00:13:46.300
M-M-M-Manager!

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.140
It’s Ten-chon.

00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:50.680
W-Where am I?

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:52.680
The infirmary.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:56.690
And everyone else is...?

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:00.150
Azuma’s match will begin soon,

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.280
so I sent them back to the assembly hall.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:04.490
Is that so?

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:07.870
According to the doctor, it’s a light heat stroke.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:11.590
To think that I’d faint from just that level of heat...

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.700
It’s really pathetic.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.380
Sweltering heat that was over 40°C,

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:20.210
and pressure from most of the audience.

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:23.890
You continued to knead the flour with that for 3 hours.

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:26.220
It’s not surprising that you fainted.

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:28.220
Rest for now.

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:31.900
Manager.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.570
I lost, didn’t I?

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:36.030
Yeah.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:40.230
I can’t fight Azuma, can I?

00:14:40.570 --> 00:14:43.480
I really want to fight it out with you, Kawachi.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.150
We can do it, right?

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:47.120
Of course.

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:50.400
I broke... my promise.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:55.670
However, even though you kneaded
that much, the flour didn’t even firm up.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.870
I’m not the only one who
thinks that something is wrong.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.890
By the Meister’s orders, your
dough is currently being analyzed.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:07.090
There’s a possibility of a
rematch depending on the results.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:09.420
Nothing will change, even with a rematch.

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:13.100
For sure, that dough was strange...

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:15.390
Someone may have tampered with it.

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:18.930
However, I’m almost a full-fledged artisan myself.

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:21.400
When I compete with someone...

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:23.440
I can figure out his level
of expertise, at least.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.200
Kanmuri Shigeru...

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.940
His skill is amazing.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.660
No matter what native yeast I have,

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:34.450
right now, I don’t feel like I can win at all.

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:39.960
I have no wish to be shamed again.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:43.300
Kawachi...

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:47.720
Azuma-san...

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:50.930
I wonder if Kawachi is all right.

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:52.430
He’s fine.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:54.600
It appears to be just a light heat stroke.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:56.440
Manager’s with him, too.

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:58.480
That’s not what I mean.

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:02.600
I’ve been working with Kawachi for a while now.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.190
That’s why I know...

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:07.070
The feeling you have when you
can’t make your bread to the very end...

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:12.620
Kawachi...

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:15.370
He tried so very hard...

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:23.510
You’ve won, so what’s with that face?

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:25.370
No reason.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:26.710
It’s just that...

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:30.010
should something also happen
to the dough in the next round,

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:32.310
everyone is going to be suspicious.

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:34.340
I’m not that much of an idiot,

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:37.890
and you don’t need to be so worried.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.890
As for the other filthy cockroach...

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.860
he seems to be self-destructing over there.

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:46.570
Kawachi...

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:53.490
Stand up!

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:54.740
Suwabara-san.

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:57.790
I’m really upset about him losing as well,

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:02.130
but don’t tell me that your
ability to fight has also vanished!

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:04.880
You...

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:06.920
Please stop!

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.380
Shut up!

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:13.130
At the employment exam
for the Main Store,

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:15.640
after being beat by you guys that time,

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:19.110
do you know what I had to go
through before making it here?

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:21.810
I... I...

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:23.350
Damn it,

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:24.810
another failure.

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:27.030
Why is it?

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:31.820
My Solar Gauntlets are at their best, and yet...

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:36.410
The moon came out!

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:39.120
The crescent moon that floats in the night sky!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.910
I can’t surpass that croissant...

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:48.050
the abominable 324 layer croissant
that Azuma and Kawachi made together.

00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:50.380
Kai.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:51.460
Master.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:53.390
Please forgive me.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:56.470
Right now, I don’t even have time to swing my sword.

00:17:57.850 --> 00:17:58.810
That’s right,

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:02.860
there are two men that I absolutely have to defeat.

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:06.650
Cool your head, Kai.

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:07.480
Master...

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:12.650
I have not come to bring you back
to the path of the sword.

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:16.190
I have come to beat that twisted
heart of yours back into shape.

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:18.780
I do not know much about bread...

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:20.030
However!

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:23.790
If you just get angry and bothered,
the true road will not appear before you.

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:27.710
Only after things cool down, will you
be able to see the true shine of an object.

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:30.210
Only after things cool down...?

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:33.170
It is just like the blade of a sword.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:38.100
Its true shine can be achieved
only after heating and cooling it.

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:47.480
The true shine...

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.930
I see it, Master,

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:15.920
and I have finally completed it.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:20.800
My Super Vapor Action six
hundred forty-eight-layer croissant!

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:23.800
Super Vapor Action 648 layer croissant!

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:28.520
Super Vapor Action something something something...?

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:31.070
It’s a rather long name.

00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:38.110
If you are a man, come meet
my challenge with all that you have.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:40.830
If you can’t do that, then just forfeit!

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:50.970
Are you all right?

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:54.710
It’s because I know
just how much Kawachi

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:57.590
wanted to win against the Main Branch in this battle.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:19:59.760
It’s frustrating...

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:01.340
and sad...

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:02.590
and mortifying.

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:05.680
Azuma-san...

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:09.350
Kawachi’s feelings seem to be

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:11.610
flowing into me, and...

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:14.610
I’m... I’m...

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:16.860
What should I do?

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:19.320
Azuma-san, it’s all right.

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:21.030
It was hard, wasn’t it?

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:23.500
You don’t have to push yourself to fight.

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:26.130
It’s all right to run away.

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:28.620
I’ll protect you.

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:30.750
Tsukino...

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:33.120
What are you blabbering about?!

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:37.340
How can you let Tsukino protect you?!
It should be the other way around!

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:40.720
Hadn’t we decided to protect her?!

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:42.840
K-Kawachi!

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:44.390
However...

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:49.020
It’s not very convincing when it comes from someone

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:51.350
who couldn’t even keep his promise.

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:55.000
Hey, Azuma.

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:57.490
You’re a kind person.

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:01.860
You were thinking of my
feelings and mourning with me, right?

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:04.120
But...

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:06.870
if you really want to share my feelings,

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:09.580
won’t you win?

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:11.620
Kawachi...

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:13.580
I’m a mediocre person.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:16.890
I may have the dreams,
but in reality, I can’t do much.

00:21:17.550 --> 00:21:20.220
For Tsukino, or even my own family,

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:22.720
it doesn’t look like I can do anything right now.

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:24.130
But...

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:26.230
you’re different, right?

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:28.090
You’re a genius!

00:21:28.810 --> 00:21:29.640
It’s not difficult.

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:33.640
For now, all you have to do is make a delicious bread.

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:36.110
The best <i>Japan</i> ever.

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:43.430
Okay.

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:47.370
We’ll now begin the semifinals for the

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:49.620
newcomers’ battle, A group.

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:56.780
From the Southern Tokyo Branch:
Azuma Kazuma.

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:59.680
From the Pantasia Main Store:
Suwabara Kai.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.000
Step forward.

00:22:06.390 --> 00:22:08.510
Come on, Azuma, move it.

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:11.470
I’ll do it...

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:13.520
Did you say something?

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:16.270
I’ll make it.

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:18.230
For Tsukino’s sake...

00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:20.230
for Kawachi’s sake...

00:22:20.780 --> 00:22:23.230
and for the sake of
Southern Tokyo Branch,

00:22:23.950 --> 00:22:26.990
the experimental, historical,
supreme <i>Japan</i>.

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:31.000
<i>Japan</i> #44.

00:22:54.480 --> 00:22:56.240
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.360
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:58.360 --> 00:23:00.360
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.660
The answer for now is...

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:04.580
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.370
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:08.160
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:18.260
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:21.140
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:23.180
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:24.590
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:29.390
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:31.230
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:36.780
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:57.590
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:05.760 --> 00:24:06.630
Finally...

00:24:06.630 --> 00:24:08.630
It’s finally time to lift the veil.

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:09.800
What’s happening?

00:24:09.800 --> 00:24:11.390
Azuma’s going to get serious!

00:24:11.390 --> 00:24:14.430
He’s going to get serious for the very first
time since the start of the series!

00:24:14.430 --> 00:24:15.600
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:18.940 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to see it!

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.060 --> 00:24:23.290
In about 20 liters of sea water,
about one of these organisms is said to exist,

00:24:23.290 --> 00:24:25.100
Sea water 20 liters

00:24:25.530 --> 00:24:26.860
the very rare Kaiyou yeast.

00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:30.030
In 1988, the first person to
successfully isolate one was...

00:24:30.030 --> 00:24:31.740
Japanese!!

00:24:31.740 --> 00:24:33.420
Really?
